{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:35:07.318Z","ordinal":35299,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0393e1fe95dcae93016b020e89c70487d2a98f9cec02d22ddf","status":"completed","call_id":"call_5f95e7f5e5944f16a44158ad0f5417b8","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat .git/nexus-claims/PA4_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_BATCH_20261121/owner.json && rg -n 'release|claim' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:600}); text(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ffa0-c475-7561-be45-26e55293b3ca","create_time":1795296905.7790353}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15762,"sampled_through_sequence":15760,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:35:07.353Z","ordinal":35300,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a1ffa0-c475-7561-be45-26e55293b3ca","session_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","root_turn_id":"01a1ffa0-c475-7561-be45-26e55293b3ca","response_id":"resp_0393e1fe95dcae93016b020e87795487d2b7e1bdb9105169e7","usage":{"input_tokens":115000,"cached_input_tokens":114688,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":134,"reasoning_output_tokens":41,"total_tokens":115134},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":45454724,"cached_input_tokens":45200384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":40810,"reasoning_output_tokens":15072,"total_tokens":45495534},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":752678710,"cached_input_tokens":745949568,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1104225,"reasoning_output_tokens":503576,"total_tokens":753782935}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:35:07.492Z","ordinal":35301,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a1ffa0-c475-7561-be45-26e55293b3ca","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9109142e-7ad7-4907-8e64-a1c589854ef2","process_id":"56963","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .git/nexus-claims/PA4_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_BATCH_20261121/owner.json && rg -n 'release|claim' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .git/nexus-claims/PA4_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_BATCH_20261121/owner.json","name":"owner.json","path":".git/nexus-claims/PA4_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_BATCH_20261121/owner.json"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'release|claim' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md","query":"release|claim","path":"CONCURRENCY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"agent\":\"GPT-6\",\"branch\":\"v1/pa4-provider-neutral-batch\",\"since\":\"2026-11-21T00:00:00Z\",\"pid\":4149643}\n12:## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n15:- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n18:## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n20:Claims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\n24:mkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\n26:if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n37:- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n51:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n60:| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n61:| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n62:| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n63:| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n64:| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n65:| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n66:| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n67:| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n71:| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n72:| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n76:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n86:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n97:| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n102:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n110:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n111:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":32366}},"started_at_ms":1795296907492,"completed_at_ms":1795296907492}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:35:07.639Z","ordinal":35302,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20008-d177-7980-9163-38b93000912f","call_id":"call_5f95e7f5e5944f16a44158ad0f5417b8","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1421)\nTotal output lines: 38\n\n{\"agent\":\"GPT-6\",\"branch\":\"v1/pa4-provider-neutral-batch\",\"since\":\"2026-11-21T00:00:00Z\",\"pid\":4149643}\n12:## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n15:- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n18:## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n20:Claims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\n24:mkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\n26:if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first reco…821 tokens truncated…t-file claims merges first.\n88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n97:| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n102:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n110:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n111:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1ffa0-c475-7561-be45-26e55293b3ca","create_time":1795296907.6394355}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15763,"sampled_through_sequence":15760,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
